      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute $y = 2 - 3x$ into the circle equation:\n$$(x - 2)^2 + ((2 - 3x) + 4)^2 = 20 \\implies (x - 2)^2 + (6 - 3x)^2 = 20$$",
        "Factorise $(6 - 3x)^2 = 9(2 - x)^2 = 9(x - 2)^2$ to simplify:\n$$(x - 2)^2 + 9(x - 2)^2 = 20 \\implies 10(x - 2)^2 = 20 \\implies (x - 2)^2 = 2$$",
        "Take square roots:\n$$x - 2 = \\pm\\sqrt{2} \\implies x = 2 \\pm \\sqrt{2}$$\nSince $P$ lies on the line segment between $B(0, 2)$ and $C(2, -4)$, the $x$-coordinate satisfies $0 < x < 2$, so:\n$$x = 2 - \\sqrt{2}$$",
        "Substitute $x = 2 - \\sqrt{2}$ into $y = 2 - 3x$ to find the $y$-coordinate:\n$$y = 2 - 3(2 - \\sqrt{2}) = 2 - 6 + 3\\sqrt{2} = 3\\sqrt{2} - 4$$",
        "State the exact coordinates of $P$:\n$$P = \\left(2 - \\sqrt{2}, 3\\sqrt{2} - 4\\right)$$"
